# UNLOCK — Hebrew / RTL

- Hebrew-first and RTL-first are product requirements, not later polish.
- Preserve correct `dir`/layout/text alignment for learner and instructor UI.
- Avoid hard-coded directional assumptions where logical CSS properties are appropriate.
- Keep mobile-first readability and touch targets.
- Use project message/i18n conventions where present rather than scattering strings inconsistently.
- Verify mixed Hebrew/English/numbers/controls in affected UI when relevant.

Canonical decision: ADR-002.
